{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/publications/council-tax-information-letter-32026-response-to-council-tax-administration-consultation-and-other-issues","content_id":"6dff8a9a-a33f-4fe9-9f37-f25baa546372","description":"Update for local authorities on the government’s response to its council tax administration consultation and other regulatory amendments.","details":{"attachments":[{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9238999","isbn":"","title":"Council tax information letter 3/2026: Response to council tax administration consultation and other issues","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/council-tax-information-letter-32026-response-to-council-tax-administration-consultation-and-other-issues/council-tax-information-letter-32026-response-to-council-tax-administration-consultation-and-other-issues"}],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>This information letter provides an update for local authorities on the government’s response to its consultation on council tax administration.</p>\n\n<p>It summarises the key announcements from this response and the timeline for reforms.</p>\n\n<p>It also provides an update on other regulatory amendments which have been made to exceptions to council tax premiums and how premiums apply in restructured local authorities.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-04-15T13:13:57Z"}],"document_type_label":"Correspondence","documents":["<section data-module=\"ga4-link-tracker\" class=\"gem-c-attachment govuk-!-margin-bottom-6\">\n  <div class=\"gem-c-attachment__thumbnail govuk-!-display-none-print\">\n    <a class=\"govuk-link\" target=\"_self\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-ga4-link=\"{&quot;event_name&quot;:&quot;navigation&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;attachment&quot;}\" href=\"/government/publications/council-tax-information-letter-32026-respo